WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.184 --> 00:00:02.859
Now it is your turn to investigate.

2
00:00:02.934 --> 00:00:06.634
Increase mass and required hover thrust rises.

3
00:00:06.859 --> 00:00:12.059
Reduce rotor area and the ideal power requirement rises too.

4
00:00:12.159 --> 00:00:16.321
Change efficiency and the electrical energy estimate changes.

5
00:00:16.655 --> 00:00:23.455
These numbers are a simplified scientific model, not a blueprint for a human-carrying

6
00:00:23.530 --> 00:00:27.580
aircraft. The goal is understanding which trade-offs govern flight.

7
00:00:27.655 --> 00:00:32.555
The lab uses a simplified hypothetical rotor-powered aircraft.

8
00:00:32.630 --> 00:00:35.931
It is not a prediction of Tesla Roadster performance.

9
00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:41.890
Choose mass, combined effective rotor area and an efficiency assumption.

10
00:00:42.185 --> 00:00:48.110
The model first finds the force needed to support weight, then estimates ideal induced

11
00:00:48.185 --> 00:00:51.051
hover power at sea-level air density.

12
00:00:51.475 --> 00:00:58.675
In the ideal model, increasing effective rotor area reduces how rapidly air must be

13
00:00:58.725 --> 00:01:00.950
accelerated to produce a given thrust.

14
00:01:01.025 --> 00:01:06.965
That tends to lower induced power, although larger rotors can create packaging,

15
00:01:07.065 --> 00:01:09.233
structural and noise challenges.

16
00:01:09.715 --> 00:01:15.065
You can observe the calculated power and the conceptual 3D rotor size updating

17
00:01:15.165 --> 00:01:22.865
together. Efficiency assumptions affect estimated electrical demand but do not replace

18
00:01:22.965 --> 00:01:25.300
rotor aerodynamic analysis.

19
00:01:25.775 --> 00:01:32.700
We do not simulate turbulent rotor interference, gust rejection, high-altitude

20
00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:36.235
operation, motor thermal limits or battery reserves.

21
00:01:36.310 --> 00:01:41.910
The purpose is to ask better engineering questions, not to create flight-worthy design

22
00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:42.882
instructions.
